# Audio auditioned against the film but not cleared for publication.
# Keep source music out of the repo: this site is published from git, so a
# committed track is a published track — and a large binary in history cannot be
# removed without rewriting every commit after it.
# A cleared cue belongs in 3d/assets/ as a short encode; see SCORE_FILE in
# 3d/assets/film.js.
3d/music/

# Renders of the film, and the packages tools/render-film.mjs needs to make one.
# Same reasoning as above: the site is published from git, so a committed render
# is a published one — a ~150 MB 4K master would be served to every visitor who
# guessed the path, and could not be taken back out of history afterwards. The
# film itself ships as /3d/film.html; a rendered file is for sending to people.
3d/out/
3d/tools/node_modules/
3d/tools/package-lock.json
